From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(RunningApp): read Steam's reaper arguments past the
 first NUL

_steam_launch_running() (0017) tells Steam's reaper for a launch apart by
its arguments, read from /proc/<pid>/cmdline, which separates them with
NULs. In Godot 4.7.1 get_string_from_utf8() stops at the first NUL
("Unexpected NUL character"), so only argv[0] came out, argv.size() < 2
for every reaper, and the check never found one. A Steam game started
from the library with Steam not yet running was then cut off: Steam sets
up Proton's prefix in a run of its own, its windows go, and 4 seconds
later OGUI stopped Steam while the game's own launch was starting (HW,
KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-10-19: Hades, three times). The NULs become
newlines before the decode. Checked on the device with Godot 4.7.1 and
the check's own code: Steam's reaper found, OGUI's own reaper and no
reaper not.

---
 core/systems/launcher/running_app.gd | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed

--- a/core/systems/launcher/running_app.gd
+++ b/core/systems/launcher/running_app.gd
@@ -346,7 +346,12 @@
 		var data := PackedByteArray()
 		while not file.eof_reached():
 			data.append_array(file.get_buffer(4096))
-		var argv := data.get_string_from_utf8().split(char(0))
+		# The arguments are NUL-separated, and get_string_from_utf8() stops at the first NUL
+		# ("Unexpected NUL character"): only argv[0] came out, so no reaper ever matched.
+		for i in data.size():
+			if data[i] == 0:
+				data[i] = 10
+		var argv := data.get_string_from_utf8().split("\n")
 		if argv.size() < 2 or argv[1] != "SteamLaunch":
 			continue
 		if argv[0].begins_with("/usr/share/opengamepadui/"):
